WEBVTT

00:01.860 --> 00:04.520
This is the weather forecast for the
Tokyo area, as released at 1 PM...

00:04.630 --> 00:07.750
...by the Meteorological Agency's
Forecasting Department.

00:07.860 --> 00:13.630
As of 11 AM on the 21st, the large
and powerful Typhoon 32...

00:13.740 --> 00:15.640
...was in the southernmost parts
of Shizuoka Prefecture...

00:15.740 --> 00:19.900
...heading northeast
at speeds of 45kph.

00:20.010 --> 00:23.410
Everyone is advised to
use extreme caution...

00:43.170 --> 00:47.300
Its winds are presently in
the 54kph range...

00:47.400 --> 00:52.970
...and caution is advised for the
Tokyo Metropolitan Area...

01:12.590 --> 01:18.060
<i>Let's chase our dreams...</i>

01:18.170 --> 01:23.270
<i>... holding hearts burning...</i>

01:23.340 --> 01:27.670
<i>... like the summer sunshine.</i>

01:27.780 --> 01:31.610
<i>If we have courage...</i>

01:31.710 --> 01:34.770
<i>... at 100 miles an hour...</i>

01:34.880 --> 01:42.880
<i>... I'm sure the door will open.</i>

01:42.990 --> 01:50.030
<i>Since sadness is the road</i>
<i>that leads to smiles...</i>

01:50.100 --> 01:58.740
<i>... dull, dingy shoes will</i>
<i>start to shine, too.</i>

01:58.840 --> 02:05.440
<i>The most wonderful dream</i>
<i>in the world...</i>

02:05.550 --> 02:12.080
<i>The pounding beat speeds up.</i>

02:12.190 --> 02:19.250
<i>The eyes are prisms that</i>
<i>catch the wind...</i>

02:19.360 --> 02:27.170
<i>... and in the voices of</i>
<i>countless friends...</i>

02:27.270 --> 02:34.000
<i>... I feel happiness.</i>

02:36.950 --> 02:39.380
FILE. 2
TOKYO TYPHOON RALLY

02:47.790 --> 02:52.820
Oh, man, I've had it. It's been
like this every week this year.

02:53.360 --> 02:56.690
Nothing we can do about it. We're up
against Mother Nature, after all.

02:56.870 --> 02:59.300
Oooh! This summer I was sure I was
gonna lose a little more weight...

02:59.400 --> 03:02.270
...take on a 1-kg parfait, heft the
Sumida Festival palanquin...

03:02.370 --> 03:03.530
...and at the night stalls, buy apple candy
and fried octopus balls in seaweed...

03:03.640 --> 03:05.070
...and baked corn and
fresh radish pickles...

03:05.170 --> 03:06.660
...and go goldfish-catching and balloon
dart-throwing and target shooting...

03:06.780 --> 03:08.740
...and shelltops... and then, uh,
brown sugar candy, oh, hey!

03:08.840 --> 03:10.830
Okay, okay. We're moving.

03:12.710 --> 03:17.310
Aw, there's no point
to anything now...

03:17.420 --> 03:19.980
Hmh? Miyuki, pull
over to the left.

03:20.160 --> 03:21.990
Huh? Okay...

03:22.090 --> 03:24.720
Students of Wakaba Preschool, please
go straight home immediately.

03:24.830 --> 03:30.030
Don't go anywhere else. There's
a scary typhoon on the way.

03:30.470 --> 03:33.330
Wow! It's Natsumi!
It's Miyuki!

03:33.500 --> 03:34.560
Hey!

03:34.740 --> 03:38.600
What's with this "Natsumi" stuff?
That's "Miss Natsumi" to you!

03:38.770 --> 03:40.800
Well, your name is
Natsumi, right?

03:40.980 --> 03:42.000
Ri-ight?

03:42.180 --> 03:43.940
It's enough for us to call
you Natsumi, right?

03:44.110 --> 03:44.740
Yeah, yeah.

03:44.910 --> 03:48.280
Hey, hey, Miyuki, do you know where
there's an animal hospital?

03:48.450 --> 03:52.480
Huh? A vet? I'm not sure if
there is one in this area...

03:52.650 --> 03:54.420
You don't even know that?

03:54.590 --> 03:57.150
Some policewoman
you are.

04:02.900 --> 04:04.590
"...Preschool"

04:03.000 --> 04:07.690
Huh? Isn't that Chibi?
You sure got big.

04:07.870 --> 04:09.600
Do you know this
cat, Natsumi?

04:09.770 --> 04:13.760
Hey, how do you know?
Huh?

04:13.940 --> 04:18.680
There is nothing that Natsumi the hero
doesn't know. Are you impressed?

04:18.850 --> 04:21.580
You can't
fool us with that.

04:21.680 --> 04:25.780
Don't
belittle the masses!

04:25.950 --> 04:28.450
What's going on? Are you
keeping her, Maho?

04:28.620 --> 04:31.220
Uh-uh. She came to the preschool
a little while ago.

04:31.390 --> 04:34.230
She's not feeling well. She
doesn't eat anything.

04:34.600 --> 04:37.290
So that's why you wanted to take
her to the hospital, huh?

04:37.470 --> 04:37.990
Uh-huh.

04:38.170 --> 04:39.600
I get it now.

04:39.770 --> 04:40.860
Oh, it's Ken!

04:41.040 --> 04:46.840
Kennie's here! Kennie's here!
Kennie's on his motorcycle!

04:46.940 --> 04:48.170
Kennie! Kennie! Kennie!

04:48.340 --> 04:51.710
Oh, so Nakajima is "Kennie"
around here?

04:51.880 --> 04:52.850
Sort of...

04:56.180 --> 04:58.410
What's this? She's
awfully fat...

04:58.590 --> 05:01.450
Stop that! You've got
to hold her properly.

05:02.160 --> 05:04.130
Oh, uh, I see...

05:04.290 --> 05:05.990
All right, we'll see that
she's taken care of.

05:06.160 --> 05:07.090
Will she be okay?

05:07.260 --> 05:12.330
We'll take care of it. We promise.
So you all hurry home. Go on!

05:21.110 --> 05:21.970
Look out!

05:24.880 --> 05:29.480
Hey! Where'd you learn to drive?! Don't
mess around like that, you idiot!

05:29.650 --> 05:32.020
Natsumi's scary!

05:32.990 --> 05:35.080
That Lancia... it's
got to be!

05:35.260 --> 05:37.220
Umm... Nakajima...

05:46.130 --> 05:50.800
I'm now going to catch
that ill-mannered car!

05:53.980 --> 05:57.100
So take care, everyone!

06:00.080 --> 06:01.840
Oh, he fell over!

06:02.020 --> 06:03.980
That GSX...

06:18.170 --> 06:21.100
I see, I see. I knew it all the time,
uh-huh, uh-huh.

06:21.270 --> 06:25.330
Oh, cut it out, Natsumi. You're
just jeering at us both.

06:25.440 --> 06:26.960
You're no better than
those preschoolers.

06:27.080 --> 06:30.440
Thanks to whom, we blew our
chance to catch that Lancia!

06:30.610 --> 06:34.810
Well, well, nice change of subject.
Won't work on me, though.

06:35.320 --> 06:36.940
Natsumi!

06:37.120 --> 06:38.420
Welcome back!

06:38.520 --> 06:40.650
You're done for the day, right?

06:40.820 --> 06:42.480
Yeah. We've done
our nightshift.

06:42.820 --> 06:45.990
Hey, hey, Nakajima's looking
a little funny.

06:46.090 --> 06:47.320
You know anything
about it?

06:47.500 --> 06:49.520
Oh! Not you too, Yoriko!

06:55.540 --> 06:57.030
Something DID happen,
didn't it!

06:57.210 --> 06:58.330
It sure did!

07:06.610 --> 07:10.480
I guess this will do for now.

07:11.520 --> 07:14.850
But you know, Nakajima
didn't look at all happy.

07:14.960 --> 07:17.790
He just went and locked
himself in the morgue.

07:17.960 --> 07:19.450
I bet he was just blushing.

07:19.630 --> 07:20.650
Oh!

07:20.760 --> 07:22.920
Are you gonna have kittens?

07:23.100 --> 07:23.860
Eh?!

07:24.030 --> 07:25.690
Oh, yeah! Her breasts are big!

07:25.870 --> 07:27.560
That's why she's so listless!

07:27.740 --> 07:29.430
So that's it!

07:29.870 --> 07:31.700
Kobayakawa!

07:32.010 --> 07:34.700
I need to ask you something.
Please come!

07:35.210 --> 07:37.180
Uh... Okay.

07:39.380 --> 07:41.180
Hey, hey, "something
to ask" must be!

07:41.350 --> 07:43.750
A proposal. It's got to be!

07:43.920 --> 07:46.510
Who'd have thought they'd
have gotten that close!

07:46.690 --> 07:47.660
It's a big scoop.

07:47.820 --> 07:48.690
We're tagging along, right?

07:48.860 --> 07:49.380
Oh, let's.

07:49.560 --> 07:51.390
All right!

08:00.900 --> 08:04.800
The rain's pouring down so loud, I can't
hear what they're talking about at all.

08:04.970 --> 08:07.600
Who cares what they're talking about?
It's actions that matter!

08:07.710 --> 08:09.370
Go! Go get 'er, Nakajima!

08:09.610 --> 08:13.740
You're the only one I can
ask this of. I beg you!

08:13.920 --> 08:16.750
For something like that,
I'll gladly assist you.

08:16.850 --> 08:21.480
And besides, there are a couple others
who look like they'll help... right?

08:40.010 --> 08:42.000
Natsumi! Bring that toolbox!

08:42.180 --> 08:43.470
Uh, right!

08:44.010 --> 08:47.210
Yoriko! There's an auxiliary flashing
light and radio! Bring them here!

08:47.380 --> 08:47.920
Uh, right!

08:47.920 --> 08:49.620
Uh, right!
Natsumi, I need a speaker too!

08:49.620 --> 08:49.750
Natsumi, I need a speaker too!

08:49.750 --> 08:50.620
Huh? Where is it?
Natsumi, I need a speaker too!

08:50.620 --> 08:50.790
Huh? Where is it?

08:50.790 --> 08:52.090
Huh? Where is it?
On the highest shelf in the back!

08:52.090 --> 08:52.220
On the highest shelf in the back!

08:52.220 --> 08:54.390
Okay, here you go.
On the highest shelf in the back!

08:54.390 --> 08:54.520
Okay, here you go.

08:54.520 --> 08:55.520
Okay, here you go.
Now get me some grease.

08:55.520 --> 08:55.660
Now get me some grease.

08:55.660 --> 08:57.630
Uh, right, right!
Now get me some grease.

09:00.760 --> 09:02.700
I'm pooped.

09:02.860 --> 09:03.560
Hey!

09:03.560 --> 09:04.330
Hey!
Eh?

09:04.500 --> 09:06.690
Thanks.

09:06.870 --> 09:08.500
Thanks for doing
this all for me...

09:08.670 --> 09:12.110
Uh-uh, no problem. I can't do
anything useful anyway...

09:12.270 --> 09:14.870
But I'm a little disappointed,
you know?

09:15.040 --> 09:20.140
So this is what your request turned
out to be? Oh, and we were sure...

09:20.310 --> 09:21.940
Huh? What did you
think it was?

09:22.320 --> 09:25.380
Eh? Uh, well, um...
Never mind that.

09:25.490 --> 09:28.150
Are you really going to go out there
using a..."KLE," was it...

09:28.260 --> 09:29.420
...as a police motorcycle?

09:29.520 --> 09:33.390
Even you wouldn't stand a chance in
the middle of a typhoon like this.

09:33.560 --> 09:37.400
I know it's risky. I have
my reasons...

10:00.990 --> 10:02.290
What condition are
the victims in?

10:02.460 --> 10:05.860
I don't know, but the ambulance
should already be on its way.

10:06.030 --> 10:09.050
Tell Nakajima that the
bike's finished.

10:09.230 --> 10:10.720
And see that the cat gets fed.

10:10.900 --> 10:12.200
Cat food and water, right?

10:47.270 --> 10:50.930
I used to enjoy typhoons,
you know?

10:51.110 --> 10:53.900
Now we can't just enjoy
them, can we?

11:03.750 --> 11:07.150
Mini Patrol Four calling Bokuto Station!
How long before the ambulance arrives?

11:07.690 --> 11:10.950
Well... the roads are badly flooded,
and it seems to be taking a detour.

11:11.060 --> 11:13.150
Looks like it'll take another
ten minutes or so.

11:13.330 --> 11:15.390
Roger! We'll figure something
out! Miyuki!

11:15.560 --> 11:16.530
I know!

11:22.070 --> 11:24.440
It's gonna be all right now.
Natsumi! Hurry!

11:24.610 --> 11:26.660
It's locked! Hang on a sec!

11:29.580 --> 11:31.200
Wha?!

11:31.380 --> 11:33.070
Now that it's come to this...

11:34.580 --> 11:37.280
...we can only exercise
brute force!

11:37.390 --> 11:39.820
Here we go...

11:39.920 --> 11:41.860
DIAMOND KNUCKLE ATTACK!

11:43.990 --> 11:44.890
I'm through.

11:46.630 --> 11:48.650
Oh wow!

12:04.910 --> 12:06.040
The watermelons are
all taken care of.

12:06.210 --> 12:07.200
Nice going. Here.

12:07.380 --> 12:09.350
Thanks.

12:11.150 --> 12:13.090
So what was the cause?

12:13.250 --> 12:15.220
Well, you see...

12:16.320 --> 12:18.290
A Lancia Delta? Then the
one this afternoon?

12:18.460 --> 12:21.760
Probably... in which case, it's
just as Nakajima feared...

12:22.000 --> 12:24.860
Eh? What does "Kennie"
have to do with it? Ow...

12:26.730 --> 12:31.400
It seems it appears every year at this
time, only on days with typhoons...

12:31.510 --> 12:34.740
...a legendary car that runs through
town like it owned the place.

12:34.910 --> 12:36.840
Then, you mean, a year ago?

12:37.010 --> 12:38.810
Yes... through some
happenstance...

12:38.910 --> 12:42.610
...Nakajima met up with
and challenged it.

12:42.780 --> 12:45.010
And he lost, huh?

12:45.190 --> 12:47.950
The bike was a serious handicap! He
was up against four-wheel drive.

12:48.060 --> 12:52.080
And it was outfitted for rallying. Not
even Nakajima could beat that!

12:52.390 --> 12:55.190
So that's why he wanted the KLE 500
with foul-weather outfitting.

12:55.300 --> 12:57.590
That's Nakajima for you; he doesn't
like to lose, does he?

12:58.170 --> 13:03.130
It's not just that. The Lancia's reckless
driving escalates each year.

13:03.240 --> 13:06.040
Fact is, it didn't cause any accidents
up until last year.

13:06.140 --> 13:08.540
If left alone at the rate it's
going, next we'll have...

13:11.350 --> 13:13.280
Yes, this is Mini Patrol
Four. Go ahead.

13:13.610 --> 13:17.780
Natsumi, Miyuki, I don't know
what to do. Hurry back here!

13:33.900 --> 13:38.900
It won't eat, it makes weird high-pitched
cries... It just won't settle down!

13:39.470 --> 13:41.240
Aren't its kittens about
to be born?

13:41.410 --> 13:43.140
If so, it wouldn't be crying.

13:43.310 --> 13:45.300
Besides, it looks like
it's in a lot of pain.

13:45.410 --> 13:48.870
I thought of calling a veterinarian,
but there's all the wind and rain...

13:49.220 --> 13:53.180
We can't very well wait for the typhoon
to pass. Natsumi! Get things ready!

13:53.350 --> 13:55.720
All right! Leave it to me!

14:04.230 --> 14:05.790
Where? Say again!

14:05.970 --> 14:09.700
Saitoo Animal Hospital, 7-4
Morishita-cho, Sumida-ku.

14:09.800 --> 14:12.740
They stop examining patients at five,
but they said they'd have a look.

14:12.910 --> 14:13.870
Roger.

14:19.850 --> 14:23.110
Animal hospital? What
are those two up to?

14:48.980 --> 14:50.970
This is Bokuto Station.
Go ahead.

14:51.150 --> 14:53.810
Yoriko? What are Kobayakawa
and Tsujimoto doing?

14:54.080 --> 14:56.140
Oh, Nakajima, you see...

14:57.350 --> 14:58.110
Blackout!

14:58.290 --> 15:00.280
People will start mobbing the phone
lines. Get someone on it!

15:00.450 --> 15:01.460
The circuit's holding!

15:01.460 --> 15:03.320
The circuit's holding!
Hey! Yoriko!

15:34.760 --> 15:38.120
Looks like a breech birth. On top of
which, her pelvis seems narrow.

15:38.290 --> 15:40.280
Well, what do we do?

15:40.690 --> 15:43.820
I'm sorry, but with things the
way they are right now...

15:44.600 --> 15:46.790
Not much you can do in
a blackout, is there?

15:47.800 --> 15:50.460
Let me see if I can contact the
Veterinarians' Association.

15:50.570 --> 15:52.370
I think there'll be a place somewhere
that will take her in.

15:54.110 --> 15:55.370
Please!

15:58.850 --> 16:02.370
We didn't hear anything about a blackout.
Tell us these things ahead of time!

16:02.950 --> 16:07.350
Sorry. But things were all messed up
here, too. They still are, though...

16:07.920 --> 16:11.120
Where was that hospital
the vet referred us to?

16:11.190 --> 16:14.650
Ayase, in Adachi-ku. We can work it out
if we get to the Kosuge Interchange.

16:15.260 --> 16:18.100
Oh, Capital Expressway Six is
closed due to construction!

16:18.270 --> 16:22.500
Why you! You should tell us
things like that beforehand!

16:22.670 --> 16:25.570
Aww, it happened
three days ago!

16:25.740 --> 16:28.770
If it's closed, that means no
one's driving on it... right?

16:29.540 --> 16:31.010
Is... that so?!

16:31.880 --> 16:35.870
Mini Patrol Four is now en route to Ayase.
We will be taking Capital Expressway Six!

16:36.050 --> 16:38.810
What! Are you serious? That's...

16:38.990 --> 16:41.680
Over and out! So long!

16:43.690 --> 16:45.890
"ENTRANCE"

16:48.130 --> 16:49.220
"NO TRESPASSING"
"Bokuto Police Station"

16:51.930 --> 16:53.260
The wind's really hellacious!

16:53.430 --> 16:55.230
Feels like we're gonna
get swept away!

16:55.340 --> 16:59.430
Driving in this rain and crosswind
is a life-threatening proposition.

16:59.540 --> 17:01.010
If you're getting out, do it now.

17:01.180 --> 17:04.630
Looking to get it all to yourself?
That's not fair.

17:04.750 --> 17:06.650
This is where the fun begins.

17:06.750 --> 17:08.010
Roger!

17:28.340 --> 17:30.430
We're almost there. Hang on!

17:30.600 --> 17:31.800
What's this?

17:31.970 --> 17:33.460
What do you mean?

17:33.640 --> 17:37.810
I thought it was a little bit strange, to see
such a gentle expression on your face.

17:38.680 --> 17:40.700
What're you talking about?

17:40.810 --> 17:44.810
It's much stranger for you to be doing
something this outrageous!

17:45.590 --> 17:47.320
That makes us even, huh?

17:48.590 --> 17:49.360
What is it?

17:49.360 --> 17:50.250
What is it?
There's a car behind us!

17:50.720 --> 17:51.850
No way! Huh!

17:57.300 --> 17:59.030
What the?! It's that Lancia Delta!

17:59.030 --> 17:59.760
What the?! It's that Lancia Delta!
I know!

18:00.130 --> 18:01.760
Of all the times it could
pick to show up!

18:01.940 --> 18:04.230
He's not likely to let us
go by quietly, is he?

18:14.980 --> 18:18.040
He's out of his mind! Miyuki, blow
him away with the nitro!

18:18.520 --> 18:20.420
That's impossible in
these conditions!

18:20.520 --> 18:22.960
It's too dangerous with this wind
and this poor visibility!

18:24.020 --> 18:25.180
Besides...

18:25.360 --> 18:28.890
Oh, yeah. There's no telling
whether Chibi could take it.

18:45.750 --> 18:47.450
Miyuki! Get off at Tsutsumi Avenue!

18:47.450 --> 18:48.110
Miyuki! Get off at Tsutsumi Avenue!
Huh?

18:48.280 --> 18:50.270
Let the Lancia Delta
pass us by.

18:50.380 --> 18:52.150
At this rate, he'll mess
you up, Miyuki!

18:52.250 --> 18:54.980
Even if he follows us, we'll have the edge
down below. We'll figure something out.

18:55.160 --> 18:56.120
You're right.

19:02.130 --> 19:04.360
He's got us figured! He's
not going to let us off!

19:04.530 --> 19:05.500
Goddamn!

19:12.140 --> 19:14.470
He's a little better than I am.

19:14.640 --> 19:15.840
Miyuki...

19:17.910 --> 19:19.170
What do we do?

19:21.020 --> 19:22.640
Mini Patrol Four, do
you read me?

19:22.820 --> 19:24.080
Nakajima?!

19:24.720 --> 19:26.150
Where are you, Nakajima?!

19:26.320 --> 19:27.650
Right in front of you.

19:33.260 --> 19:35.020
Yoriko filled me in.

19:35.130 --> 19:36.860
You're carrying a patient, so you must
be having a hard time fighting him.

19:36.960 --> 19:38.120
I'll back you up.

19:38.300 --> 19:40.070
Kennie! You're so cool!

19:40.070 --> 19:41.030
Kennie! You're so cool!
Stop that.

19:46.570 --> 19:49.130
I'm the one who's taking you
on! Come and get me!

19:54.150 --> 19:56.480
Kobayakawa! It's only
5 km to Kosuge!

19:56.580 --> 20:00.210
Get into his slipstream and follow us!
His car should act as a windbreak!

20:00.390 --> 20:03.550
Will you be all right, Nakajima? Bikes are
the most dangerous in this weather!

20:03.890 --> 20:07.450
I put my faith in this bike
you tuned, Kobayakawa.

20:40.560 --> 20:43.530
Oh, man! We've already reached
the Kosuge offramp!

20:43.630 --> 20:46.960
Hey, hey, Miyuki, you've fallen for
"Kennie" all over again, I bet.

20:47.170 --> 20:49.970
Look, I told you to stop referring
to him like that.

20:50.140 --> 20:53.300
Well, how about Kenbo? Ken-Ken?
Kensuke? The Kenster?

20:53.410 --> 20:55.430
"Kennie" really is best,
don't you think?

20:55.540 --> 20:57.030
Oh! It's from "Kennie!"

20:57.210 --> 20:59.200
This is where we
part for now.

20:59.310 --> 21:02.680
I'll join you after I take
care of this clown.

21:02.780 --> 21:04.750
Take care of that
chubby Chibi.

21:12.490 --> 21:13.290
I wonder if he can win out.

21:13.460 --> 21:16.260
Sure he can! He will! Kennie
can if anyone can!

21:17.460 --> 21:21.460
Natsumi! You keep saying, "Kennie,
Kennie," and now I'm doing it, too...

21:21.640 --> 21:24.930
What's wrong with that? You're gonna
be calling him that sooner or later!

21:25.110 --> 21:28.200
How can you say that! Don't decide
such things by yourself!

21:28.480 --> 21:31.140
Whatever! Keep your
eyes on the road!

21:31.310 --> 21:32.050
Don't try to evade the subject!

21:32.050 --> 21:34.100
Don't try to evade the subject!
We're gonna crash!

21:37.820 --> 21:41.650
I repeat...

21:41.760 --> 21:46.120
...the Joban Line is currently halted
within the Tokyo city limits.

21:47.690 --> 21:53.190
It is unclear when service
will be reestablished.

22:06.110 --> 22:09.510
Right at the next corner. Then
left about 300m after that!

22:09.680 --> 22:10.580
Roger!

22:14.050 --> 22:15.920
Hang in there! It's just
a little longer!

22:19.890 --> 22:21.860
You bastard!

22:24.630 --> 22:25.830
Ah-ah!

22:30.900 --> 22:33.530
I'm not like I was last year!

22:41.920 --> 22:43.470
We can't get through here!
Where's a detour?

22:43.650 --> 22:48.850
Hold on... Back up and go left on that last
road... no good! Neither is going right!

22:49.290 --> 22:49.990
Which way?

22:49.990 --> 22:51.990
Which way?
Mmm... there is no way.

22:51.990 --> 22:52.060
Mmm... there is no way.

22:52.060 --> 22:53.290
Eh?! It can't be!
Mmm... there is no way.

22:53.460 --> 22:56.990
With this much water, it's all the same
no matter which way you go!

22:57.160 --> 22:59.690
Getting around this will mean
going way out of our way.

22:59.870 --> 23:04.200
Which means we only have one option
left... Natsumi, you're on!

23:04.340 --> 23:06.430
I had a feeling it would
come to this.

23:11.680 --> 23:14.480
All set. Natsumi, this
is the final hurdle.

23:14.950 --> 23:18.320
No problem. My bike technique
can stand up to this typhoon!

23:19.190 --> 23:20.150
Yeah!

23:23.290 --> 23:24.260
Go!

24:02.560 --> 24:04.550
I've got something to say
to you. Listen up!

24:04.730 --> 24:07.130
When driving near children,
maintain a safe distance...

24:07.230 --> 24:10.200
...and furthermore, go slowly!
Remember that.

24:31.630 --> 24:34.860
"Animal Hospital"

25:18.810 --> 25:22.100
"This is a present for good children.
Pick it up gently."

25:55.610 --> 25:58.440
"Miss Natsumi, Miss Miyuki,
Thank You"

26:28.740 --> 26:37.080
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

26:37.150 --> 26:46.490
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

26:46.590 --> 26:54.500
<i>The sunset skyline flashes past</i>
<i>in my side-view mirror.</i>

26:54.570 --> 27:02.060
<i>This is the road I drive on every day,</i>
<i>believing in my dreams.</i>

27:02.180 --> 27:09.980
<i>On rainy days, windy days, and days</i>
<i>when I wanted to throw it all away...</i>

27:10.080 --> 27:17.750
<i>... you smiled as you</i>
<i>sat beside me.</i>

27:19.030 --> 27:23.530
<i>I love the unchanging vista, the sky</i>
<i>that we watch together.</i>

27:27.530 --> 27:34.340
<i>That's why I'm confident that I can</i>
<i>hang in there, if it's for you.</i>

27:34.410 --> 27:42.810
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

27:42.920 --> 27:43.050
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

27:49.390 --> 27:49.420
<i>I love this town where we</i>
<i>happened to meet...</i>

27:52.930 --> 27:57.230
Honestly, those kids... Miyuki,
this isn't coming off!

27:57.400 --> 27:59.560
Look, just put some elbow
grease into it.

27:59.670 --> 28:01.430
We'll clean her up even
if it takes all day.

28:01.600 --> 28:04.970
Eek! No way!

28:06.810 --> 28:09.300
"THE TRUTH BEHIND
THE RUMORS"

28:09.080 --> 28:12.480
Why are you having a matchmaking, when
you have someone like Nakajima?

28:12.980 --> 28:13.510
Want me to tell?

28:13.510 --> 28:16.110
Want me to tell?
Hey, who are you talking about?

28:16.280 --> 28:19.250
Stop her, Nakajima! You're the
only one who can stop Miyuki!

28:19.420 --> 28:21.110
Look, what are you
talking about?

28:21.290 --> 28:21.950
Wanna know?

28:22.120 --> 28:24.610
You want her to be taken away by
some nobody from nowhere?

28:24.790 --> 28:26.850
How did you come up
with a story like that?

28:27.030 --> 28:28.050
Shall I tell you?

28:28.230 --> 28:29.990
So you're the cause of all this!

28:30.160 --> 28:33.460
You're Under Arrest, File 3,
"Love's Highway Stars."

28:33.630 --> 28:36.800
FILE. 3
LOVE'S HIGHWAY STARS
